{"parentUuid":"44942dcf-78d3-4e4f-9038-d8dbcd444795","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"22277250-1783-45bc-9d5b-e32f754ab6c5","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01JNoR7bZtLjAo2dTivf85QB","type":"tool_result","content":"- **Expected reports: 35.3.** That's each stratum's draw times the report rate eval A and lexicon v2 judged in it (decisions 27, 30 and 31), summed. The rules' strata pool their judged items, which are too few apart. Adding each stratum's Wilson ends gives 14.0 to 86.5, which is wider than the total's own interval.\n  - E6 holds no judged item and E8 one, so the 35 counts none of their reports. Under `POLICY.md` a sighting of a phantom ship (rule 14) and an exposed hoax (rule 7) are reports.\n  - The judged labels predate `POLICY.md`, and rule 2 turns one of eval A's `other` into a report.\n  - **For field-level intervals:** at 35 reports, a field right in 30 of them has a Wilson interval of 71–94%. About 50 reports would take about 70 more articles in v1's headline stratum, out of the near misses, the bulk and the early decades. I kept those, since they measure triage, the bulk's kinds, and B8's early decades.\n- **Decades in gold:** 22 before 1850, then 12, 15, 17, 29, 52, 50, 46 and 39 for the 1850s to the 1920s, then 9, 6, 1 and 2 for the 1930s to the 1960s.\n- **Inclusion weights:** each article's `pi`, its stratum's draw over its size, and its `weight`, 1/`pi`, are in `split.json`. Gold's candidate weights sum to 1,235,182, every candidate less the 940 in `POLICY.md`'s example groups. A near miss stands for 267,832 of the near-miss pool's 6,695,792.\n- **Dev:** 150 articles, gold's design at half the size, drawn from outside gold's groups. No dev article reprints a gold one by whole text, so none was redrawn.\n  - **I label dev by hand under `POLICY.md`, in 2C.2, alongside gold and before any model output.** Model selection then aims at the same truth as gold, not at the teacher's labels the student learns from.\n- **`POLICY.md`'s examples:** 63 articles. 60 are candidates, and they and their groups, 944 articles, are left out of gold and dev.\n  - The other 3 are lexicon v1's random samples from eval A's screen, in no file the draw reads.\n  - `check_leakage.py` compares all 63 with gold and dev by whole text, and none is reprinted there.\n- **The pool:** 1,539,818 articles: every candidate and near-miss reservoir article outside the 6,567 held out. Those are gold, dev, their groups, the quarantine and its groups.\n  - 2C.4 draws the teacher-labelled training data from the pool, at most one printing per story.\n  - The random reservoir stays out of training, since eval B screens it for recall.\n- **`check_leakage.py` exits 0** (`eval/results/phase2c/leakage.json`): no group crosses the split, no pool article reprints a gold or dev one, no dev article reprints a gold one, no example is drawn or reprinted, and `HASH` matches.\n- **The labelling page** (`scripts/label_gold.py`) runs on 127.0.0.1 only.","is_error":false}]},"uuid":"8d3300cb-09b9-4b0e-86b7-7612495b459a","timestamp":"2026-10-31T07:20:07.792Z","toolUseResult":{"stdout":"- **Expected reports: 35.3.** That's each stratum's draw times the report rate eval A and lexicon v2 judged in it (decisions 27, 30 and 31), summed. The rules' strata pool their judged items, which are too few apart. Adding each stratum's Wilson ends gives 14.0 to 86.5, which is wider than the total's own interval.\n  - E6 holds no judged item and E8 one, so the 35 counts none of their reports. Under `POLICY.md` a sighting of a phantom ship (rule 14) and an exposed hoax (rule 7) are reports.\n  - The judged labels predate `POLICY.md`, and rule 2 turns one of eval A's `other` into a report.\n  - **For field-level intervals:** at 35 reports, a field right in 30 of them has a Wilson interval of 71–94%. About 50 reports would take about 70 more articles in v1's headline stratum, out of the near misses, the bulk and the early decades. I kept those, since they measure triage, the bulk's kinds, and B8's early decades.\n- **Decades in gold:** 22 before 1850, then 12, 15, 17, 29, 52, 50, 46 and 39 for the 1850s to the 1920s, then 9, 6, 1 and 2 for the 1930s to the 1960s.\n- **Inclusion weights:** each article's `pi`, its stratum's draw over its size, and its `weight`, 1/`pi`, are in `split.json`. Gold's candidate weights sum to 1,235,182, every candidate less the 940 in `POLICY.md`'s example groups. A near miss stands for 267,832 of the near-miss pool's 6,695,792.\n- **Dev:** 150 articles, gold's design at half the size, drawn from outside gold's groups. No dev article reprints a gold one by whole text, so none was redrawn.\n  - **I label dev by hand under `POLICY.md`, in 2C.2, alongside gold and before any model output.** Model selection then aims at the same truth as gold, not at the teacher's labels the student learns from.\n- **`POLICY.md`'s examples:** 63 articles. 60 are candidates, and they and their groups, 944 articles, are left out of gold and dev.\n  - The other 3 are lexicon v1's random samples from eval A's screen, in no file the draw reads.\n  - `check_leakage.py` compares all 63 with gold and dev by whole text, and none is reprinted there.\n- **The pool:** 1,539,818 articles: every candidate and near-miss reservoir article outside the 6,567 held out. Those are gold, dev, their groups, the quarantine and its groups.\n  - 2C.4 draws the teacher-labelled training data from the pool, at most one printing per story.\n  - The random reservoir stays out of training, since eval B screens it for recall.\n- **`check_leakage.py` exits 0** (`eval/results/phase2c/leakage.json`): no group crosses the split, no pool article reprints a gold or dev one, no dev article reprints a gold one, no example is drawn or reprinted, and `HASH` matches.\n- **The labelling page** (`scripts/label_gold.py`) runs on 127.0.0.1 only.","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false,"bashEditDiff":{"files":[{"filePath":"/Users/hotragn/Documents/Claude Code/HacktoberFest/week4/Paperghosts/Docs/DECISIONS.md","hunks":[{"oldStart":831,"oldLines":7,"newStart":831,"newLines":7,"lines":["   - The rule flags all 603 one-story pairs of the randomly drawn strata. The lowest share is 0.105 (`dev-0088`) and the fewest shared runs is 6, so the rule sits just under both.","   - The large clusters' least similar pairs are the hardest by construction, and eval A's links group them anyway.","   - It flags 12 of the 17 randomly drawn pairs of two stories, since those pairs share passages. A false flag only keeps an article out of training.","-  - **It earned its place.** Outside their groups, 1,196 pool articles reprint 142 of the 450 gold and dev articles. Most are short repeated texts: mediums' cards and patent-medicine adverts re-run in later issues, steamer timetables, market columns, and wire passages two papers share. An advert of 50 words holds about six seven-word runs, of which one in eight is kept, so it rarely shares the two runs a link needs.","+  - **It earned its place.** Outside their groups, 1,196 pool articles reprint 142 of the 450 gold and dev articles. Most are short repeated texts: mediums' cards and patent-medicine adverts re-run in later issues, steamer timetables, market columns, and wire passages two papers share. An advert of 50 words has about 40 seven-word runs, of which one in eight is kept, so a few OCR errors leave it without the two shared runs a link needs."," - **The strata** (`scripts/gold_draw.py`, `eval/results/phase2c/gold_draw.json`). A candidate falls in the first that fits:","   1. **Three edge-case slices** the archive holds too few of to meet by chance (SRS 7.3), found by pattern: phantom ships, trains and lights (E8), hoaxes and pranksters (E6), and text not in English (E12). The other eleven slices are common among candidates, and 2C.2 counts each slice on the labels.","   2. **Before 1850:** 2.2% of candidates. A proportional share would be about 7 of 300, too few for B8's decade slices."]},{"oldStart":863,"oldLines":7,"newStart":863,"newLines":7,"lines":[" ","   Articles are each stratum's size outside `POLICY.md`'s example groups. For near misses it's the near-miss pool the reservoir stands for. The five rules' rows share the rate their judged items pool."," ","-- **Expected reports: 35.3.** That's the sum, over the strata, of the report rates eval A and lexicon v2 judged (decisions 27, 30 and 31). The rules' strata pool their judged items, which are too few apart. Adding each stratum's Wilson ends gives 14.0 to 86.5, which is wider than the total's own interval.","+- **Expected reports: 35.3.** That's each stratum's draw times the report rate eval A and lexicon v2 judged in it (decisions 27, 30 and 31), summed. The rules' strata pool their judged items, which are too few apart. Adding each stratum's Wilson ends gives 14.0 to 86.5, which is wider than the total's own interval.","   - E6 holds no judged item and E8 one, so the 35 counts none of their reports. Under `POLICY.md` a sighting of a phantom ship (rule 14) and an exposed hoax (rule 7) are reports.","   - The judged labels predate `POLICY.md`, and rule 2 turns one of eval A's `other` into a report.","   - **For field-level intervals:** at 35 reports, a field right in 30 of them has a Wilson interval of 71–94%. About 50 reports would take about 70 more articles in v1's headline stratum, out of the near misses, the bulk and the early decades. I kept those, since they measure triage, the bulk's kinds, and B8's early decades."]}]}],"moreFiles":0,"changedFiles":["/Users/hotragn/Documents/Claude Code/HacktoberFest/week4/Paperghosts/Docs/DECISIONS.md"]}},"serverClassifierContext":{"request":"7d28aa52-f8af-455a-a249-d6063b0379cc","context":{"git_state":{"cwd":"/Users/hotragn/Documents/Claude Code/HacktoberFest/week4/Paperghosts","root":"/Users/hotragn/Documents/Claude Code/HacktoberFest/week4/Paperghosts","branch":"phase-2c-reader","default_branch":null,"s